mindmap
  root(("QA/QC 2026+"))
    FIX 1 - Testing vs QA §1.2.2 v4.0.1
      QA: process-oriented, preventive; good process leads to good product; covers development and test processes; everyone's responsibility; uses test results as process feedback
      Testing: product-oriented, corrective; a major form of quality control, others are formal methods, simulation, prototyping; uses test results to fix defects
    Static testing CTFL ch.3
      What: examines work products without executing them; reviews - informal, walkthrough, technical review, inspection; static analysis by tools
      Where it fits: a form of testing, product-oriented and corrective; shift-left from the first work products; used in test analysis to evaluate the test basis; finds defects directly while dynamic testing causes failures §3.1.3
      Review process §3.2.2: planning, review initiation, individual review, communication and analysis, fixing and reporting
    Branch 1: ISTQB CTFL v4.0.1 test process §1.4
      Test planning
        Tasks: define test objectives; select test approach within constraints
        Work products: test plan, test schedule, risk register, entry and exit criteria
      Test monitoring and control
        Tasks: check progress against the plan; evaluate exit criteria; take control actions
        Work products: test progress reports, documented control directives, risk information
      Test analysis: what to test
        Tasks: analyse test basis; identify testable features; define and prioritise test conditions with risks; evaluate test basis for defects and testability
        Work products: prioritised test conditions e.g. acceptance criteria; defect reports on the test basis
      Test design: how to test
        Tasks: elaborate test conditions into test cases; identify coverage items; define test data requirements; design test environment and tools
        Work products: prioritised test cases, test charters, coverage items, test data and test environment requirements
      Test implementation
        Tasks: create testware and test data; organise procedures into suites; write manual and automated scripts; arrange execution schedule; build and verify environment
        Work products: test procedures, test suites, automated test scripts, test data, test execution schedule, stubs, drivers, simulators, service virtualisation
      Test execution
        Tasks: run tests per schedule; compare actual and expected results; log results; analyse anomalies and report defects
        Work products: test logs, defect reports
      Test completion
        Tasks: change requests for unresolved defects; archive or hand over testware; shut down environment to agreed state; lessons learned; completion report
        Work products: test completion report, improvement action items, lessons learned, change requests or backlog items
      Cross-cutting: iterative or parallel and tailored to context §1.4.2; traceability §1.4.4
      FIX 2 - Roles in testing §1.4.5
        Test management role: test planning, test monitoring and test control, test completion
        Testing role: test analysis, test design, test implementation, test execution
    Branch 2: QA/QC job roles 2026
      FIX 2 - Mapping to ISTQB roles: QA lead = test management role; manual tester, SDET, AI/LLM QA tester = testing role; quality engineer = both; process QA = QA, outside the two testing roles
      Manual tester
        Responsibilities: analyse requirements; design test cases; exploratory and regression testing; log defects with severity and priority; retest
        Skills: EP, BVA, decision table, state transition; domain knowledge; Jira, Postman, SQL basics; clear written English
      Automation engineer / SDET
        Responsibilities: build UI and API automation; integrate tests into CI/CD; triage flaky tests; performance scripts
        Skills: Playwright, Selenium, Cypress; TypeScript, Java or Python; REST/GraphQL; Git, Jenkins, Docker; JMeter or k6
      AI/LLM QA tester
        Responsibilities: test chatbots, RAG and AI features; check accuracy, grounding, hallucination, consistency; test bias, safety, prompt injection; build evaluation datasets; check EU AI Act needs
        Skills: prompt engineering; LLM evaluation metrics; Python and data testing; OWASP Top 10 for LLM applications
      QA lead
        Responsibilities: test strategy, plan, estimation; entry and exit criteria, release risk; lead testers; report metrics; govern GenAI use
        Skills: test management, risk-based testing, leadership, stakeholder communication
      Quality engineer
        Responsibilities: quality across the whole SDLC; CI/CD quality gates; shift-left and shift-right; observability
        Skills: automation and API testing; contract testing e.g. PACT; observability tools; SQL; AI-assisted testing
      Process QA
        Responsibilities: define and audit processes against standards; track non-conformities and corrective actions; process metrics and improvement
        Skills: ISO 9001, CMMI, ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119; audit techniques; root cause analysis
    Branch 3: AI impact per role
      Manual tester
        REPLACE: bug report formatting, test data variants
        ASSIST: FIX 3 - test case drafts; partitions and boundaries for review, ambiguity spotting, log analysis
        CANNOT: exploratory testing, UX judgement, defect vs intended behaviour, real devices
      Automation engineer / SDET
        REPLACE: boilerplate scripts, locators, page objects, self-healing locators
        ASSIST: flaky test debugging, CI failure triage, refactoring
        CANNOT: framework architecture, what to automate, reviewing AI assertions
      AI/LLM QA tester
        REPLACE: large prompt-variant datasets, first-pass LLM-as-judge scoring
        ASSIST: red-teaming prompts, clustering failures, computing metrics
        CANNOT: ground truth and thresholds, harm and bias judgement, regulatory accountability
      QA lead
        REPLACE: status dashboards
        ASSIST: FIX 3 - report drafts; estimation, risk brainstorming, test plan drafts
        CANNOT: go/no-go decision, people management, stakeholder negotiation
      Quality engineer
        REPLACE: routine quality-gate checks
        ASSIST: telemetry anomaly detection, test impact analysis
        CANNOT: quality strategy, risk appetite, business impact
      Process QA
        REPLACE: collecting process metrics, template compliance checks
        ASSIST: audit evidence review, RCA drafts
        CANNOT: audit interviews, judging real adoption, compliance sign-off
